DATA USE TERMS

This repository supports the Tri-CEA project, "Harnessing Controlled Environment
Agriculture to Secure Sustainability and Economic Growth," an NSF EPSCoR-funded
collaboration across New Mexico, Wyoming, and South Dakota and their tribal
communities. Consistent with the project's Data Management Plan, use of this
data is subject to the following:

1. Indigenous Data Sovereignty. Data from or about tribal communities remains
   under the governance of those communities. Users must respect tribal nations'
   rights to control how data about their people, lands, and resources is used,
   and must not use it in ways that harm or misrepresent them.

2. Human-Subjects Data. Social and survey data are shared only in aggregate to
   protect privacy. Do not attempt to re-identify individuals or reveal personal,
   demographic, or disability information about participants.

3. FAIR Principles. Data is shared following FAIR (Findable, Accessible,
   Interoperable, Reusable) best practices. Please preserve the associated
   metadata when reusing or redistributing data.

4. Attribution. Please cite the Tri-CEA Project (https://tricea.unm.edu) when
   using this data in publications, presentations, or derivative works.
